[134,'What should be reviewed before allowing alerts to bind to CIs in non-operational lifecycle states?','Business need, status configuration, ownership, and risk of misleading impact','Only the visualization style used to display the Alert','Only the connector’s display name without its source behavior','Only the number of characters in the incoming Node value','Changing lifecycle exclusions affects operational accuracy and routing.','CI Binding Governance'],
[135,'A Kubernetes alert identifies a pod rather than a traditional host. What binding approach is recommended?','Use Event Rule CI field matching with appropriate non-host CI context','Rely only on default host Node matching','Create a server CI for every pod name','Bind to the MID Server','Non-host cloud-native objects need class-aware matching.','CI Binding Configuration'],
[136,'What should an event-source data contract specify for reliable binding?','Node semantics, class/type, identifiers, field formats, and lifecycle expectations','Only the source display name','Only Alert Severity','Only connector ownership','The contract must define how source identity maps to CMDB identity.','CI Binding Governance'],
[137,'Why should CI class values be normalized rather than accepted as arbitrary source text?','They must map predictably to approved CMDB classes','They control dashboard themes','They replace identifiers','They set Incident urgency','Governed class mapping prevents invalid or unsafe table searches.','Event Field Mapping'],
[138,'Which TWO teams should jointly own CI Binding quality? (Choose 2)','Monitoring integration owners who control event identity','CMDB and service owners who control CI identity and lifecycle','Catalog authors only','CAB attendees only','Binding spans source data and CMDB data, so both sides must govern it.','CI Binding Governance',['Monitoring integration owners who control event identity','CMDB and service owners who control CI identity and lifecycle']],
[139,'What should a binding-remediation runbook include?','Source checks, Processing Notes, Event Rules, field mapping, CMDB search, lifecycle, and escalation','Only a dashboard screenshot without source or processing evidence','Only the Alert number without its Event or CI context','Only the connector credential without diagnostic or escalation steps','A repeatable path should trace identity from source through CMDB match.','CI Binding Operations'],
[140,'What demonstrates production readiness for CI Binding?','Representative sources consistently bind positive cases correctly, reject ambiguous cases safely, and expose measurable failures','One manually bound alert without testing repeat events or negative binding cases','A nonempty Node value on every event regardless of whether it identifies a valid CI','An active dashboard that reports raw event volume but not binding accuracy or failures','Readiness requires accuracy, safe failure, observability, and operational ownership.','CI Binding Testing']
